"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[88295],{788295:e=>{e.exports='# Production Apply\n\n## Planning Mode\n\nGiven migration context (git vs non-git, original job ID, cloned job ID), report:\n\n| Step       | Git                                            | Non-git                                         |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Job config | `editAsset` on production job                  | Same                                            |\n| Notebooks  | `gitCommitAndPush` to branch; updates on merge | `editAsset` to overwrite original, delete clone |\n| Cleanup    | Delete cloned working-copy job                 | Same                                            |\n\n## Execution Mode\n\n1. `editAsset` — apply serverless config to the production job. The agent\n   must mutate the job spec so each task has serverless compute attached;\n   leaving classic-compute fields cleared but `environment_key` unset\n   produces a task with no compute target that hangs at run time.\n\n   **Precondition — verify no hidden init-script infra to translate.**\n   Before applying the example below, inspect the source task\'s\n   `new_cluster` (inline) and any `job_clusters[]` entry it references\n   via `job_cluster_key` for `init_scripts`. If `init_scripts` is\n   non-empty, STOP and require `infrastructure-translation` to run\n   first — that skill is what produces the `environments[]` entry with\n   the translated init-script dependencies. Other cluster-level fields\n   (`libraries`, `policy_id`, `spark_conf`, `spark_env_vars`) are\n   currently outside `infrastructure-translation`\'s scope (see its\n   "Routing per Cluster-Level Field" table — they\'re flagged to the\n   user, not translated). If any of those are present, follow\n   `infrastructure-translation`\'s flagging guidance separately; do not\n   silently drop them via this skill.\n\n   **For each task that passes the precondition:**\n   - Remove `existing_cluster_id`, `new_cluster`, and `job_cluster_key`.\n   - Set `environment_key` to point at an entry in the job-level\n     `environments[]` array.\n\n   **At the job level:**\n   - Add an entry to `environments[]` with the matching `environment_key`\n     and a `spec` containing `environment_version`. The\n     `environment_version` value must be derived from the source job\'s\n     DBR `spark_version` — see the canonical mapping table in\n     `infrastructure-translation/init-scripts.md` (Step 9: "Reference in\n     Job Config"). Do **not** hardcode a value; pick the one that\n     matches the source.\n   - Remove `job_clusters[]` entries that are no longer referenced by\n     any remaining task.\n   - Preserve all other top-level job fields (`name`, `schedule`,\n     `tags`, `email_notifications`, etc.) — `editAsset` mutates only\n     the compute-related fields above.\n   - **Post-mutation invariants — verify before reporting success.**\n     Every task in the final job spec must satisfy **exactly one** of:\n     (a) `environment_key` set and no classic-compute fields\n     (`existing_cluster_id`, `new_cluster`, `job_cluster_key`) — task\n     migrated successfully; or (b) all classic-compute fields still\n     present and `environment_key` unset — task intentionally left on\n     classic (partial migration). If any task has **neither**\n     `environment_key` nor any classic-compute field, it has no\n     compute target and the run will hang — STOP with an error. If\n     any task is in state (b), surface a partial-migration warning to\n     the user before reporting success.\n\n   \x3c!-- TODO: replace inline example with `readSkillFile(\'infrastructure-translation\')` once that skill documents a no-infra path. --\x3e\n\n   **Example — minimal job (no cluster-level infra to translate):**\n\n   Before — using `existing_cluster_id` (all-purpose cluster):\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     "tasks": [\n       {\n         "task_key": "main_task",\n         "existing_cluster_id": "0123-456789-abcdef01",\n         "notebook_task": { "notebook_path": "/path/to/notebook" }\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Before — using `job_clusters[]` + `job_cluster_key` (scheduled job):\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     "job_clusters": [\n       {\n         "job_cluster_key": "my_cluster",\n         "new_cluster": {\n           "spark_version": "16.4.x-scala2.12",\n           "num_workers": 2,\n           "node_type_id": "Standard_DS3_v2"\n         }\n       }\n     ],\n     "tasks": [\n       {\n         "task_key": "main_task",\n         "job_cluster_key": "my_cluster",\n         "notebook_task": { "notebook_path": "/path/to/notebook" }\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n   ```\n\n   After — both Before shapes converge on the same After:\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     "tasks": [\n       {\n         "task_key": "main_task",\n         "environment_key": "serverless_env",\n         "notebook_task": { "notebook_path": "/path/to/notebook" }\n       }\n     ],\n     "environments": [\n       {\n         "environment_key": "serverless_env",\n         "spec": { "environment_version": "<derive from source DBR>" }\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n   ```\n\n   For jobs **with** infrastructure to translate (init scripts, libraries,\n   policies), `infrastructure-translation` runs earlier in the\n   orchestrator and produces the `environments[]` entry already — in\n   that case this step\'s `editAsset` applies that pre-built spec.\n\n2. **Git:** `gitCommitAndPush` notebook changes; provide compare link `{repo}/compare/master...{branch}`\n   **Non-git:** `editAsset` to overwrite original notebook with clone content; delete cloned notebook via `runDatabricksCli` → `workspace delete <cloned_notebook_path>`\n3. Delete cloned working-copy job via `runDatabricksCli` → `jobs delete <cloned_job_id>`\n\nOutput: job update confirmation (ID + link), notebook update confirmation, compare link (if git).\n'}}]);
